# Copy to .env for local use. Never commit a real .env file.
# SITE_URL is public metadata (used for canonical/OG URLs), never a secret.
# It has a safe fallback in apps/site/astro.config.mjs, so this is optional
# for local builds; set it once the real Vercel project domain is confirmed.
SITE_URL=https://diegoaleyvag.vercel.app

# Ask Diego's optional model provider (AGENTS.md, .cursor/rules/ai-guide.mdc):
# off by default, and gated to real Vercel Preview and Production
# deployments only (VERCEL_ENV === "preview" || "production") — see
# provider.ts's `createProviderFromEnv`. Production activation was an
# explicit, separate authorization made only after a passing Preview
# verification (C9A, 2026-09-05); it did not change the model, limits,
# ZDR, corpus, or any other control below. Only
# apps/site/src/pages/api/ask.ts reads these, only on the server, only
# through that single composition root — never in browser code or a
# PUBLIC_*-style variable. With either left unset, or on a
# Development/local deployment (no VERCEL_ENV=preview|production),
# /api/ask runs corpus-only and gracefully degrades to the static FAQ;
# nothing else on the site depends on them.
#
# Provider: Groq's official OpenAI-Chat-Completions-compatible endpoint
# (https://api.groq.com/openai/v1, fixed in code — not configurable here,
# so a stray env var can never redirect the key to another host).
#
# GROQ_MODEL: a Groq model id currently on the Free tier for this account.
# Verify the exact value AND its tier at https://console.groq.com/docs/models
# and the account's real quota at https://console.groq.com/settings/limits
# before setting this — model tiers move (e.g. Llama 3.1 8B Instant is
# listed as an Enterprise-only "Production Model" as of this writing, not
# Free), so no example model id is given here to avoid implying one is
# currently available. No default is provided on purpose: Groq's free-tier
# lineup and quotas are account-specific and change over time, so guessing
# one here would risk silently pointing at a model this account can't
# serve.
GROQ_MODEL=
# GROQ_API_KEY: the bearer credential for that endpoint, server-side only.
# Real value lives only in Vercel's Preview- and Production-scoped
# environment variables, never here — each environment's copy is its own
# secret, configured (and revocable) independently of the other. To
# disable the provider immediately without a redeploy, revoke/disable the
# key (or the whole Groq project)
# from the Groq console — /api/ask degrades to the corpus/fallback on the
# very next request. The hard ceiling against runaway usage is the rate
# limit the operator configures directly on the Groq project
# (console.groq.com/settings/limits), kept below the account's observed
# free-tier quota — not this app's per-session in-memory rate limiter, and
# not a payment-based spend cap (a Free-tier account has no billing method
# attached to cap spend against in the first place).
#
# Operational prerequisite before enabling the provider in any environment
# (Preview or Production): enable Zero Data Retention (ZDR) for this Groq
# account in the Groq console's Data Controls
# settings (https://console.groq.com/docs/your-data). Without ZDR, Groq
# may temporarily retain request/response content for up to 30 days for
# reliability/abuse monitoring. This application itself never logs a
# prompt, answer, IP address, or header (only bounded aggregate metrics,
# see AGENTS.md); the call to Groq is server-to-server, so Groq observes
# this server's IP, never the visitor's browser IP. ZDR does not stop
# Groq from collecting its own usage metadata (request counts, latency),
# which Groq always collects regardless — it only controls retention of
# request/response content.
GROQ_API_KEY=
